Planar 2D Detonation

OVERVIEW:

To run type:
> sh ./runsim.sh
This will execute runmpi.sh or runsbatch.sh depending on the system
To edit model parameters, number of cpus, timestep, etc.. edit this file.
This file willthen execute runmpi.sh or runsbatch.sh, depending on whether its run on the local
machine, or the slurm cluster.  To change the amount of job memory required, edit runsbatch.sh

To do post-processing run in the following order:
> sh ./post.sh
> sh ./post2.sh
> sh ./post3.sh
> sh ./post4.sh
> sh ./post5.sh
To edit which frames to run through, number of cpus to use at any given time, edit post.sh and post4.sh
by default it creates density, Schlieren, and temperature frames in png format.
Note, you can run these in the background on a local machine.  I.e. 
> nohup sh ./post.sh > postout &



-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DESCRIPTION OF FILES IN THIS FOLDER BY TYPE:

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.  SIMULATION FILES

  runsim.sh:
    This is the main simulation 'engine'.
    User can specify a) the number of cpus to use
                     b) number of loops to output
                     c) time between loops
                     d) name of model file to load (i.e. detonation2D.dat)

  2DChannel_hotspot.dat:
    This is the principle model file for the simulation
    It contains the geometry, boundary conditions, and other model parameters to use

  ffcm1_h2.cti:
    Contains the thermodynamic and reaction data based on the H2 portion of the FFCM-1 mechanism

  XInitial_ffcm.dat:
    Contains the number of moles of each species, in order of appearance in ffcm1_h2.cti

  x.dat:
    Opens an X-Window for viewing simulations

  p.dat
    Used by x.dat

  _math:
    Contains floating point math needed to run the bash scripts properly


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------


2.  POST-PROCESSING FILES


  post.sh scripts:
    Main post-processing scripts for this simulation


  makeXQframes.sh:
    Creates raw data (xq) files from the simulation.  Run as part of post1.sh

  makePNGframes.sh:
    Creates png files for density, reactant, and temperature for each simulation loop
    These are used for creating movies.  Run as part of post4.sh



-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------


3.  MISC FILES

  clear.sh:
    Clears all data generated by any previous run.

  time.sh:
    Returns the total simulation run time


